In the $\approx 0-22$ {\tt Interior} part
{\tt cam} is {\tt BEHIND} the {\tt Man=black shirt/grey
slacks} looking {\tt N/TOP} to:

* {\tt white spiral stair} = {\tt N/TOP} , on {\tt N} side of
lit {\tt DANCEFLOOR} in middle of {\tt red carpet}
* lit {\tt DANCEFLOOR} = {\tt CENTER}
* {\tt Man} himself $= {\tt S/BOTTOM}$ of {\tt FLOOR} on the
{\tt red carpet} {\tt \approx 5m S} of the {\tt FLOOR} {\tt
CENTER}
* {\tt big black pit/sofa + stage/light truss + video wall}
$= {\tt E/RIGHT}$ {\tt screen RIGHT} of {\tt FLOOR CENTER},
on the {\tt E edge} of the {\tt red carpet}, {\tt \approx
10m E} of the {\tt FLOOR CENTER}

So on the screen at $0^{s}$ :

* {\tt FLOOR CENTER} = {\tt CENTER}
* {\tt Man} = {\tt BOTTOM/CENTER}
* {\tt Sofa} = {\tt RIGHT/CENTER}

For a {\tt avatar} {\tt standing ON} the {\tt FLOOR CENTER}:

* {\tt Sofa} is $\approx 90^{o}$ {\tt E} of you on your
{\tt RIGHT} hand side {\tt screen RIGHT} if you {\tt FACE N}
to the {\tt spiral}.

* {\tt Man} is $\approx 180^{o}$ {\tt S} of you on the
{\tt BOTTOM} edge of the picture. 

> i.e. if you {\tt FACE N/TOP} to the {\tt spiral} the
> {\tt Man} is directly {\tt BEHIND} you {\tt S/BOTTOM} and
> you have to turn {\tt \approx 180^{o} BEHIND/BACKWARDS} to
> see him, if you {\tt FACE S/BOTTOM} to the {\tt cam} the
> {\tt Man} is directly {\tt FORWARD/IN FRONT} of you {\tt
> S/BOTTOM}, {\tt Sofa} then on your {\tt LEFT} hand side.
